                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:1:5adbea27",
                "summary": "Async voice failures never escalate: sayWord resets failures to 0 on every 'requested' result (src/recognise/recognise.ts:1303), while real failures arrive later via utterance.onerror, so two failed taps in a row both show 'Vorlesen ging nicht' and never 'Vorlesen geht nicht. Hol eine Bezugsperson.' (reproduced with an asynchronous failed() probe). board.ts:355-362 resets failures only on onEnd. The test (test/recognise.test.mjs:595) only calls failed() synchronously. Fix: do not reset failures on 'requested'; reset on utterance end by passing onEnd to requestLocalGermanSpeech at recognise.ts:1277 (and extend sayText for tests), keep show(null) for a word said; add a test that calls failed() after sayText returns, twice in a row, expecting the 'geht nicht' line. Paused paths, carry, switch, guard, focus and draw checked without defects.",
