                "submission_id": "submission:blindspot-review:1:8c89829c",
                "summary": "Partial-failure blind spot in owner decision (a): '▶ Weiter' from paused calls startCamera, which shows 'starting' without the tiles and, if the camera then fails (problem: busy/permission/stopped, recognise.ts:584-588,643-645,657) or the permission ask ends without a problem (leave(), recognise.ts:645), the paused tiles are gone: 'Nochmal' restarts with carried=[] (recognise.ts:685,661-663). The owner kept the tiles because they are the child's message waiting to be read; a failed resume destroys it irreversibly and no test covers it. Smallest fix: when a start that carried tiles fails or is refused, return to { kind: 'paused', taken: carry } (or keep carry for the problem view's retry), plus one controller test. Also noted: page hide/pagehide calls recogniser.back() in every state (recognise.ts:1341-1344), so a paused view (camera already off) closes and loses the tiles on screen lock, and device auto-lock (often 30 s-2 min) usually fires before RECOGNISE_IDLE_MS; docs/recognise.md 'The view stays open' does not say this. Verified fine: nothing is spoken without a tap; idle stop calls stopCamera and the test asserts camera.running false; paused hides the camera switch and keeps 'Zurück zur Tafel'; no frames buffered while paused (camera=null).",
                "task_id": "NG-55",
                "validation_references": []
            }
        },
