                "summary": "Two tile-loss paths remain. (1) recognise.ts:594 failed() pauses with own.carry, the start-time snapshot: after Weiter with [trinken], a new tile hilfe, then the camera stopping, the pause shows only [trinken] (probe-verified); a start without carry that fails while listening still drops all tiles to problem. Fix: keep current.kind==='listening' ? current.taken : own.carry, and pause when that is non-empty. (2) recognise.ts:746-753 hide() during starting with carried tiles (Weiter or switch) calls leave(): state idle, tiles lost (probe-verified), against docs/recognise.md:283. Fix: in hide(), when current.kind==='starting' and camera.carry is non-empty, stopCamera and pause with that carry. Camera is off in every probed path; countdown/recording hide, gone, dispose unchanged; 70/70 tests pass. Also: the problem lines in the pause say tap Nochmal (recognise.ts:146-155) but the pause shows Weiter.",
