                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:5:152ce6ff",
                "summary": "The bridge-null fix is correct, and each new test fails without its change (checked by mutation). One defect remains against owner decision (b). In draw() at src/recognise/recognise.ts:1108 the voice failure count (and emptyLists) is reset on every state other than listening or paused. That includes the 'starting' state shown on 'Weiter' and on a camera switch. So a failure, then 'Weiter', then a second failure shows 'Vorlesen ging nicht' again instead of 'Vorlesen geht nicht. Hol eine Bezugsperson.'. A probe test reproduced this. The owner's rule is that the count resets only when an utterance ends, and docs/recognise.md:295 says the same. Fix: reset failures, emptyLists and lastTaken only on idle (the end of the message), or keep them while starting. Add a test for a failure, then 'Weiter' or a switch, then a failure. No other path loses the tiles or leaves the camera on.",
